  "description": "What: CE-1967 (user report: a bulldozer driving over soldiers only knocked them down; they stood up after it passed) - on bt-range a 49 t bulldozer (TKB 112) drives north from (150,130) to (150,175) at 4.5 m/s, its top speed, WITHOUT giving way to anyone - a RamTarget at a place (the mover's avoidance gives way to no person), as the user's possessed dozer drove; \u26a0 an ordinary MoveToLocation steers round a standing man (measured: the hull passed 4 m beside him); 'Victim' stands on its line at (150,145), 'Bystander' 7 m east of it at (157,145); both hold (no brain reaction, so the run-over is not avoided by the man). Judge: the dozer reaches its point; the Victim is DEAD once the hull has passed over him (a heavy hull crushes what it drives over, R-2138) and never stands up again; the Bystander, beside the 4.3 m blade, is untouched. Fail: the Victim alive after the dozer passed (the defect), or the Bystander hurt. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh ua-dozer-runover"
